From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:47:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MLD STA: send Action frames to the AP MLD on an enabled link

wpa_supplicant sends each Action frame to the AP on the frequency of
the association link. An established advertised TID-to-link mapping
can disable that link, and mac80211 then sends the frame there by a
remain-on-channel. IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 35.3.7.2.1: "If a link is
disabled for a non-AP MLD, it shall not be used for individually
addressed frame exchange ..., including Management and Control
frames". The frame also goes on the association link where it answers
a request that the AP MLD sent on another link.

35.3.14.1 makes the SA Query, WNM Sleep Mode, BSS Transition
Management, SCS, MSCS and FT Action frames intended for the MLD, so
they may use any enabled link. Every other individually addressed
frame is intended for the STA of one link, and goes through another
link only with an MLO Link Info element (35.3.14.3), which
wpa_supplicant does not build.

Send the frames intended for the MLD, and the frames that the station
sends unprompted (BSS Transition Management Query, Neighbor Report
Request, MBO WNM Notification, WFA Capabilities, DSCP Policy Query),
with no frequency, so that the driver picks an active link. A frame
with an OCI keeps the association link, since its OCI names that
link's channel. Send the Radio Measurement Report, the Link
Measurement Report and the solicited DSCP Policy Response on the
frequency on which the request arrived. Do not let the nl80211 driver
send a frame to the AP MLD off-channel: a frame for a link that is not
active, such as a disabled one, is refused.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -10209,6 +10209,12 @@ static int wpa_driver_nl80211_send_action(struct i802_bss *bss,
 		      drv->nlmode == NL80211_IFTYPE_NAN_DATA))
 		offchanok = 0;
 
+	/* A frame to the AP MLD goes on an active link or not at all, since a
+	 * link that is not active can be disabled (IEEE 802.11be 35.3.7.2.1) */
+	if (is_sta_interface(drv->nlmode) && drv->sta_mlo_info.valid_links &&
+	    ether_addr_equal(dst, drv->sta_mlo_info.ap_mld_addr))
+		offchanok = 0;
+
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 		   "nl80211: Send Action frame (ifindex=%d, freq=%u MHz wait=%d ms no_cck=%d offchanok=%d dst="
 		   MACSTR " src=" MACSTR " bssid=" MACSTR ", link_id=%d)",
